@page "/about"

<PageTitle>About - @SiteInfo.Title</PageTitle>
<HeadContent>
    <meta name="description" content="About @SiteInfo.Title: @SiteInfo.Description" />
</HeadContent>

<article class="post">
    <h1>About</h1>
    <div class="post-content">
        <p>
            Hi, I'm Gergroen. This is my developer blog with short, practical <strong>getting started guides</strong>,
            mostly about .NET, C# and the tools around them.
        </p>
        <p>
            Every guide aims to take you from nothing to a small working example, with all the code you need.
        </p>
        <h2>About this site</h2>
        <p>
            This blog is a <a href="https://dotnet.microsoft.com/apps/aspnet/web-apps/blazor">Blazor WebAssembly</a> app,
            hosted on GitHub Pages. Posts are plain Markdown files in the
            <a href="@SiteInfo.RepositoryUrl">GitHub repository</a>. You can install it as an app on your device and read
            posts you've opened before while offline.
        </p>
        <p>
            <a href="@SiteInfo.GitHubUrl">GitHub</a> · <a href="feed.xml">RSS feed</a>
        </p>
    </div>
</article>
